{
 "_about": "Map of every sprite sheet. Cell = column index 0..3. Crop each cell between the title band (top) and the caption band (bottom). 'mirror' = flip horizontally after cutting. 'use': false = do not export for the engine. 'derive' = make this frame by mirroring another frame. 'erase' = boxes [x0, y0, x1, y1] in pixels of the cell (x from the cell's left edge, y from the top of the sheet) that are painted white before cutting. 'fix_white': true = take back white face fur that the background remover ate (use only where a notch shows in the forehead or muzzle). Sheets with a transparent background are detected automatically: their figures are found by shape, left to right, and 'remove_marks', 'erase' and 'fix_white' are then not needed. 'rows': number of rows of figures on a transparent sheet (figures are read row by row, left to right).",
